message.content:
{"diagnosis": "Loopback send 0xa5 with divider 64 trapped as uart data mismatch got 0xff want 0xa5. ser_tx is driven low during reset because send_pattern resets to ~1 whose LSB is 0 instead of idle-high ~0, injecting a false start on loopback. This desyncs recv_state/recv_pattern sampling so the real frame is missed and RX holds idle 0xff.", "patch_diff": "diff --git a/picosoc/simpleuart.v b/picosoc/simpleuart.v
--- a/picosoc/simpleuart.v
+++ b/picosoc/simpleuart.v
@@ -113,7 +113,7 @@
 		if (!resetn) begin
-			send_pattern <= ~1;
+			send_pattern <= ~0;
 			send_bitcnt <= 0;
 			send_divcnt <= 0;
 			send_dummy <= 1;", "expected": "tohost PASS (not FAIL 0xdead), no uart data mismatch trap, loopback got 0xa5"}

